{"name":"Deep Seaweed","hex":"#37412a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deep","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extending, reaching or positioned far from a point of reference, especially downwards.\nExtending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively.","Extending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Far, especially far down through something or into something, physically or figuratively.","In a profound, not superficial, manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep"},{"term":"seaweed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of numerous marine algae, such as a kelp.","Any of various fresh water plants and algae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seaweed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Seaweed","blocks":[{"text":"Seaweed, or macroalgae, refers to thousands of species of macroscopic, multicellular, marine algae. The term includes some types of Rhodophyta (red), Phaeophyta (brown) and Chlorophyta (green) macroalgae. Seaweed species such as kelps provide essential nursery habitat for fisheries and other marine species and thus protect food sources; other species, such as planktonic algae, play a vital role in capturing carbon and producing at least 50% of Earth's oxygen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Fucus_serratus_2015-09-08_ag_M0010140.jpg/330px-Fucus_serratus_2015-09-08_ag_M0010140.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seaweed"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Ascophyllum_nodosum.jpg/500px-Ascophyllum_nodosum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Ascophyllum_nodosum.jpg/500px-Ascophyllum_nodosum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o